<h2>How much time does each take?</h2>
<p>For AI video from photos, the work starts as soon as we have the photos. There is nothing to schedule on your side. We make up to 2 videos a day, and the delivery date is agreed with you before we start. A person watches every video in full before you see it.</p>
<p>A filming day starts with finding a date. For a yacht, that means a day in port, clean and without guests, in the season when most boats are out. For a hotel, it means empty, made-up rooms and quiet public areas. After the shoot comes the edit. If the weather turns or a room is not ready, the date moves.</p>

<h2>What does each cost?</h2>
<p>Our price is per video and includes VAT. A single video costs €100. From 5 videos it is €95 per video, and the price drops by €5 for every 5 videos, down to €50 per video. A free 15 to 25 second preview comes first, and you pay by bank transfer within 14 days of the invoice. See the <a href={pagePath(lang, 'pricing')}>full price ladder</a>.</p>
<p>A filming day is priced differently, and quotes vary widely between production companies and regions, so we do not give a figure here. The main cost drivers are:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>The crew day rate.</strong> Camera operator, sometimes an assistant or a director, for one or more days.</li>
  <li><strong>Travel.</strong> Getting the crew and equipment to a marina or a hotel, and sometimes accommodation.</li>
  <li><strong>Editing.</strong> Selecting footage, grading colour, adding music and making the different cuts.</li>
  <li><strong>A drone pilot.</strong> For aerial shots, often with permits depending on the location.</li>
  <li><strong>Reshoots.</strong> If the weather fails or a shot is missing, another day on location.</li>
</ul>
<p>For one flagship property, a filming day can be worth it. For a fleet of yachts or a hotel with many room types, those costs repeat for every yacht or every visit.</p>

<h2>What can AI video from photos not do?</h2>
<p>It is important to be clear about this. A video made from photos:</p>
<ul>
  <li>shows only what is in the photos. A room, a cabin or a view that was never photographed cannot appear;</li>
  <li>has no people in it, and we do not add guests or crew;</li>
  <li>has no recorded sound from the scene;</li>
  <li>works best with calm, slow camera moves. Large changes of angle make the AI guess, and guesses can look wrong;</li>
  <li>is only as good as the photos. Sharp, well-lit, high-resolution photos give the best film.</li>
</ul>

<h2>When is a filming day the better choice?</h2>
<p>A filming day is the better choice if you want:</p>
<ul>
  <li>people in the shot: guests on deck, staff at work, a chef in the kitchen;</li>
  <li>real sound or an interview with an owner, a captain or a manager;</li>
  <li>drone footage of places you have no photos of;</li>
  <li>rooms or areas that have never been photographed;</li>
  <li>a brand film with a story, rather than a walkthrough.</li>
</ul>
<p>If any of these matter to you, we would rather say so than sell you something that cannot do it.</p>

<h2>When is AI video from photos the better choice?</h2>
<p>It fits when you already have good photos and want a calm walkthrough for each listing: every yacht in a fleet, every room type in a hotel, every rental in a portfolio. It also fits when you cannot easily free a yacht or a room for a day, or when you want a video now rather than after the season.</p>
<p>You do not need any skills or software. You send a link or the photos, we make the film, and you get MP4 files in 16:9 and 9:16, with two revision rounds. Read more about <a href={pagePath(lang, 'aiVideo')}>how AI video from photos works</a>.</p>

<h2>Can you combine them?</h2>
<p>Yes. You could film one flagship video for your home page and use AI video from photos for the rest of your listings. The two do not exclude each other.</p>

<h2>Try it with your own photos</h2>
<p>The quickest way to compare is to see your own photos in motion. We make a free preview of 15 to 25 seconds, with a few shots from your listing photos, with no obligation. <a href={pagePath(lang, 'contact')}>Send us a link to your listing</a>.</p>
